// The GO block goes on into a state that a transition leads back to when that transition can never fire (S never
// terminates, so T is never entered): KIELER leaves the dead block out of the state's guard, which is then _GO, and
// its conditional merger joins the code with the root's. m = o + 1 names no input and runs in reset() before o =
// twice(x): KIELER gives m = 1.
scchart Main {
  input int x
  output int o, m
  method int twice(int v) { return v * 2 }
  initial state S { dataflow once { o = twice(x) m = o + 1 } } join to T
  state T go to S
}
